 "summary": "This is an unusually ambitious hard SF novel that uses the conceit of a generation ship's institutional memory as a vehicle for a sustained argument about epistemic honesty, bureaucratic self-deception, and the maintenance of truth across centuries. Its first half is genuinely gripping narrative fiction with psychologically complex characters; its second half becomes something closer to institutional chronicle, trading dramatic momentum for thematic depth and elegiac scope. The voice is the book's greatest achievement \u2014 a dry, engineering-inflected prose that never wavers and that makes its rare emotional moments land with disproportionate force.",
